{
  "id": "ticket_01KY93E2NTZ7WK156HEQRVKCN1",
  "name": "distribution broken: npm/npx slop cannot run without Bun; dist binary single-platform and unpublished",
  "slug": "distribution-broken-npm-npx-slop-cannot-run-without-bun-dist",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "bin.slop points at raw src/cli/index.ts (shebang #!/usr/bin/env bun), so npm i -g / npx produces a slop that fails without a pre-existing Bun; Node cannot strip TS types under node_modules. dist/slop (the real artifact) is unused by bin, gitignored-but-in-files, un-built by any publish step, and a single-platform 100MB binary.",
    "details_md": "Reproduced on Node v25.9.0: env: bun: No such file or directory (exit 127); node <path> -> ERR_UNSUPPORTED_NODE_MODULES_TYPE_STRIPPING. engines only sets bun, so npm prints no warning. This is the npm package’s entire reason to exist (D2).",
    "acceptance": [
      "A user can install and run slop via the documented channel on macOS/Linux without separately installing Bun, OR the distribution is explicitly and truthfully scoped (e.g. Bun-only / curl installer) and npm metadata/README stop implying Node compatibility",
      "If dist/slop is published, a prepublishOnly/prepack builds it and per-platform artifacts are selected at install; no dead-weight wrong-platform binary ships",
      "A smoke check installs the package into a clean prefix and runs slop --version successfully"
    ],
    "context": [
      "package.json:7-9 bin, :16-18 engines, :12-15 files",
      "src/cli/index.ts:1 shebang",
      ".gitignore dist/ vs files: [dist]",
      "no prepublishOnly/prepack script; .github/workflows/ci.yml never publishes"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
